description.narrative:
The African Centre for the Constructive Resolution of Disputes (ACCORD) will undertake a series of activities and dialogues to unpack the contemporary challenges to multilateralism and discuss opportunities for a reinvigoration of conflict prevention and peacebuilding in Africa.

These activities and dialogues align with Denmark’s United Nations Security Council (UNSC) elected term of 2025-2026. Denmark's term will focuses on equality, security and action. Denmark will use the membership opportunity to:
•	Prioritise international law and a more effective and representative Security Council; 
•	Look into conflict responses and prevention fit for new realities;
•	Focus on climate peace and security; and 
•	Women, peace and security.

ACCORD proposes to use the SDG funds available via the Danish Embassy for the following:
•	Seminar focused on Prioritising Equality, Security and Action with African countries;
•	Roundtable/Webinar on Climate, Peace & Livelihoods in the SADC region linked to the African Common 
         Position on Climate Change;
•	Africa Consultation on the 2025 UN Peacebuilding Architecture Review and SG Peacebuilding Report; 
         and
•	WPS Lessons Learned (UN Resolution 1325 25th anniversary) reflections on prevention of, and 
         accountability for conflict related sexual violence.
